    "result": "# Ponytail - AI Code Agent Overview\n\n## What It Does\nPonytail is an agent skill designed to prevent AI coding assistants from over-engineering solutions. It implements a decision-making \"ladder\" that agents must follow before writing any code, encouraging minimal implementation.\n\nThe project personifies this approach as \"the laziest senior dev\" - someone who would replace fifty lines with one line when possible.\n\n## Key Features\n\n### Decision Ladder\nBefore writing code, the agent evaluates options in this order:\n1. Does this need to exist? (YAGNI principle)\n2. Is it already in this repo? (reuse it)\n3. Does the standard library do it?\n4. Does the platform do it?\n5. Does an installed dependency do it?\n6. Can it be one line? (write the line)\n7. Only if nothing above applies: write the minimum that works\n\n### Reported Metrics\n- 54% less code generated\n- 20% cheaper to run\n- 27% faster execution\n- Up to 94% less code on tasks where agents typically over-build\n- 100% of safety guards maintained (validation, error handling, security, accessibility)\n\n### Commands\n- `/ponytail [lite|full|ultra|off]` - Set intensity level\n- `/ponytail-review` - Review current diff\n- `/ponytail-audit` - Audit entire repository\n- `/ponytail-debt` - Collect deferred shortcuts\n- `/ponytail-help` - Quick reference\n\n## Installation\nInstall via npm:\n```bash\nnpm install -g @0xwilliamortiz/ponytail-improved\nponytail\n```\n\nOr without global install:\n```bash\nnpx @0xwilliamortiz/ponytail-improved\n```\n\n## Compatibility\nWorks with multiple AI coding tools including Claude Code, Codex, Copilot CLI, OpenCode, Cursor, and others. Requires Node.js on PATH for full functionality.\n\n## Release Information\n- License: MIT\n- Repository: 0xwilliamortiz/ponytail-improved\n- Status: Active project with plugin configurations for various AI coding platforms\n- GitHub stars: 599, forks: 129",
    "durationMs": 6789,
    "url": "https://github.com/0xwilliamortiz/ponytail-improved"
  }
}

