        "tool_use_id": "call_fdd1193645314fc88edae2d4",
        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "# Nepali IDE: AI-Native Mobile Code Editor for Android\n\n## Overview\nNepali IDE is a mobile integrated development environment created by Diwas Khatri that brings desktop-class coding to Android devices. It features a code editor with syntax highlighting, embedded Python interpreter, live HTML preview, and AI assistance powered by Google Gemini.\n\nThe application follows MVVM architecture using Kotlin and Jetpack Compose with Material 3 design, offering local SQLite storage through Room for project management and file versioning.\n\n## Key Features\n\n### AI-Powered Development (Google Gemini)\n- **AI Code Completion**: Context-aware suggestions powered by the Gemini API directly in the editor\n- **AI Code Analysis**: One-tap intelligent code review identifying bugs, optimizations, and best practices\n- **AI Unit Testing**: Automatic test generation for code with a single click\n- **AI Assistant Panel**: Dedicated chat-style drawer for brainstorming, debugging, and code explanation with Gemini\n\n### Smart Code Editor\n- Syntax highlighting for Python, HTML/CSS, and web languages\n- Multi-tab editing with instant file switching\n- Full undo/redo support and auto-save functionality\n- Find & replace bar for quick refactoring\n- Custom keyboard toolbar with common coding symbols\n- VS Code-style command palette\n- Live cursor position and file information status bar\n\n### Built-in Interpreters & Live Preview\n- Python interpreter that runs scripts directly on device without server\n- Interactive REPL console for code experimentation\n- HTML live preview rendering in built-in web view\n\n### Project Workspace & Data\n- Multiple project creation, organization, and switching\n- File tree drawer supporting create, rename, delete, and snippets\n- Automatic version snapshots with restore capability\n- Visual SQLite database browser for table and record inspection\n- JSON formatting and validation tools\n- CSV data viewing\n- Cross-project snippet library\n- Built-in todo task tracker\n\n### Git Integration\n- Commit changes with messages\n- Track history\n- Manage workspace through built-in Git panel\n\n### Theming & UX\n- Multiple editor color schemes\n- Modern Material 3 design\n- Project dashboard with file overview and activity statistics\n\n## Technical Architecture\nBuilt on clean MVVM architecture with single-activity Jetpack Compose design:\n\n**Tech Stack**:\n- Language: Kotlin 1.9+\n- UI: Jetpack Compose + Material 3\n- Database: Room (SQLite) for local persistence\n- AI/LLM: Google Gemini API with Firebase GenAI, Retrofit + OkHttp\n- Concurrency: Kotlin Coroutines + Flow\n- Serialization: Moshi for JSON parsing\n- Interpreter: Custom Kotlin Python implementation\n- Testing: JUnit + Roborazzi + Compose Test\n- Build: Gradle Kotlin DSL + KSP\n\n## Project Structure\nThe app organizes code into:\n- `ai/`: Gemini AI models and repository\n- `data/`: Room entities, DAOs, WorkspaceRepository\n- `editor/`: SyntaxHighlighter and EditorTheme\n- `interpreter/`: PythonInterpreter and HtmlPreviewView\n- `ui/components/`: All Compose UI components\n- `ui/theme/`: Material 3 theming\n\n## Setup Requirements\n- Android Studio Koala or newer\n- JDK 17+\n- Android SDK 35+\n- Gemini API key from Google AI Studio\n\n## Roadmap\nPlanned features include PHP/JavaScript interpreters, GitHub sign-in with cloud sync, collaboration mode, additional language syntax themes, terminal emulator, Firebase Analytics, and Google Play Store publication.\n\n## License\nMIT License\n\nThis project demonstrates that \"world-class developer tools can be built locally\" by a Nepali developer using modern Android development practices."
      }
