    "result": "# Dev Workspace - Memory for Coding Agents\n\n## Product Overview\n\nDev Workspace is a markdown-based knowledge base template designed to address a critical gap in AI-assisted development: **agents excel at writing code but struggle with remembering why decisions were made**. Chat history disappears, and the reasoning behind design choices evaporates with it.\n\n## Key Features\n\n### Open Knowledge Format (OKF) Compliant\nThe workspace adheres to the Open Knowledge Format v0.2 standard, ensuring your project graph remains portable across different OKF-consuming tools rather than being locked to a single platform.\n\n### Structured Graph Architecture\nEvery document includes typed frontmatter with:\n- Document type classification\n- Provenance tracking (generated vs. sources)\n- Lifecycle metadata (status, stale_after)\n- Schema validation via `iwe schema validate` in CI\n\n### Organized Document Structure\nThe workspace contains specialized directories for different aspects of development:\n\n- `index.md` - Graph root and entry point\n- `product.md` - Product definition\n- `plans/` - Implementation plans tracked through stages\n- `features/` - Feature documentation from proposal to implementation\n- `bugs/` - Bug tracking with symptoms, reproduction steps, root causes, and fixes\n- `spec/` - Behavioral specifications synchronized at ship time\n- `architecture/` - Design decisions including rejected alternatives\n- `concept/` - Product vision documentation\n- `codebase/` - Component tree and data flows\n- `releases/` - Version tracking and unreleased changes\n- `backlog/` - Prioritized upcoming work\n- `someday/` - Ideas without commitments\n- `milestones/` - Plans containing child plans\n\n## How It Works\n\n### Initial Setup\nThe template includes an automated setup skill that reads your existing codebase and drafts initial documentation, asking questions only when code analysis cannot provide answers.\n\n### Continuous Workflow\nThe workspace supp