      {
        "tool_use_id": "call_1dccb235ee8249b0b637489d",
        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "# Antigravity CLI VS Code Extension Overview\n\n## Purpose and Integration\n\nThis VS Code extension \"integrates the `agy` (Antigravity CLI) AI coding assistant into your editor environment.\" Rather than requiring users to \"switch to a separate terminal window,\" it opens `agy` as \"a right-side editor panel—keeping your code visible on the left and the AI assistant on the right.\"\n\nThe extension is specifically designed to mirror \"the UX of Claude Code and Codex extensions, but is purpose-built for the Antigravity CLI.\"\n\n## Key Features\n\n| Feature | Description |\n|---------|-------------|\n| Activity Bar Icon | Left sidebar icon that opens the welcome panel |\n| Right-Side Terminal | Opens as editor tab on right, not bottom panel |\n| Top-Right Button | Icon in each editor's top-right corner |\n| Status Bar Item | \"AGY indicator at the bottom-left—always visible\" |\n| Keyboard Shortcut | `Cmd+Shift+A` (Mac) / `Ctrl+Shift+A` (Windows/Linux) |\n| Smart Reuse | Focuses existing terminal instead of duplicates |\n| Auto-Close | Terminal closes when user runs `/exit` in `agy` |\n| Configurable | Supports custom `agy` path and default launch arguments |\n\n## Version 0.0.2 Update\n\nThe latest version introduced drag-and-drop support for adding files to CLI context. Users can drag files \"from the VS Code Explorer into the active Antigravity terminal\" by holding the `Shift` key to paste the absolute path.\n\n## Installation Methods\n\n### Marketplace Installation\nThe extension is published on VS Code Marketplace; users can search for \"Antigravity CLI\" in the Extensions panel or install directly via the marketplace link.\n\n### VSIX Installation\nManual installation involves downloading the `.vsix` file and using the command palette to select \"Extensions: Install from VSIX...\" or running:\n\n```\ncode --install-extension antigravity-cli-0.0.2.vsix\n```\n\n### Source Installation\nAdvanced users can build from source by cloning the repository, installing dependencies with `npm install`, compiling TypeScript with `npm run compile`, packaging with `npm run package`, then installing the resulting VSIX.\n\n## Technical Requirements\n\n- VS Code v1.85.0 or higher\n- Node.js v18+ and npm (only for building from source)\n- Antigravity CLI (`agy`) installed and in PATH\n\nUsers verify installation with `agy --version`.\n\n## Configuration\n\nSettings accessible via VS Code Settings (search \"antigravity\"):\n\n- `antigravity.executable`: Path to `agy` binary (default: \"agy\")\n- `antigravity.defaultArgs`: Array of launch arguments\n\n## Project Architecture\n\nThe TypeScript-based extension uses a modular structure:\n\n- `src/extension.ts` - Main entry point handling activation/deactivation\n- `src/terminalManager.ts` - Terminal lifecycle management\n- `src/statusBarManager.ts` - Status bar state management (idle/running)\n- `src/welcomeViewProvider.ts` - Sidebar webview HTML panel\n\nCompilation outputs to `out/` directory. Debugging uses VS Code's Extension Development Host via F5 launch.\n\n## Usage\n\nMultiple access methods exist: Activity Bar icon, top-right editor button, status bar \"AGY\" indicator, keyboard shortcut, or Command Palette (\"Antigravity CLI: Open Terminal\"). Commands also support restarting and stopping the terminal."
      }
    ]
  },
