ory, installing dependencies with `npm install`, compiling TypeScript with `npm run compile`, packaging with `npm run package`, then installing the resulting VSIX.\n\n## Technical Requirements\n\n- VS Code v1.85.0 or higher\n- Node.js v18+ and npm (only for building from source)\n- Antigravity CLI (`agy`) installed and in PATH\n\nUsers verify installation with `agy --version`.\n\n## Configuration\n\nSettings accessible via VS Code Settings (search \"antigravity\"):\n\n- `antigravity.executable`: Path to `agy` binary (default: \"agy\")\n- `antigravity.defaultArgs`: Array of launch arguments\n\n## Project Architecture\n\nThe TypeScript-based extension uses a modular structure:\n\n- `src/extension.ts` - Main entry point handling activation/deactivation\n- `src/terminalManager.ts` - Terminal lifecycle management\n- `src/statusBarManager.ts` - Status bar state management (idle/running)\n- `src/welcomeViewProvider.ts` - Sidebar webview HTML panel\n\nCompilation outputs to `out/` directory. Debugging uses VS Code's Extension Development Host via F5 launch.\n\n## Usage\n\nMultiple access methods exist: Activity Bar icon, top-right editor button, status bar \"AGY\" indicator, keyboard shortcut, or Command Palette (\"Antigravity CLI: Open Terminal\"). Commands also support restarting and stopping the terminal.",
