    "result": "# Kimi K3 Code Free Desktop AI\n\n## Overview\nKimi K3 Code Free Desktop AI is a desktop application that provides free access to Kimi K3 from Moonshot AI. It's a \"free GitHub Copilot alternative\" offering substantial capabilities without subscription fees.\n\n## Technical Specifications\n- **Model:** Kimi K3 with 2.8 trillion parameters\n- **Context Window:** 1 million tokens\n- **Platform Support:** Windows 10/11, macOS, and Linux\n- **License:** MIT License (Copyright © 2026 albert3106)\n\n## Key Features\n\n### Core Capabilities\n- Terminal-based coding agent for autonomous task execution\n- Multi-file upload supporting up to 50 files simultaneously\n- IDE integration with file read/write and shell command execution\n- Extended reasoning mode for complex problem solving\n- Handles \"complete engineering tasks across large repositories\"\n\n### Technical Innovations\n- Delta Attention mechanism for \"accurate recall across the full 1M window\"\n- Kimi Code CLI tool with parallel subagent spawning\n- Built-in free tier with no API key required for basic usage\n- Superior Chinese language support described as \"best-in-class for coding\"\n\n## Installation\n\nDownload the application directly from GitHub releases:\n`KimiK3-desktop.zip` (available in the Releases section)\n\n## Local Running Option\n\nThe application supports local execution via Ollama using GGUF quantized weights. System requirements include:\n- 32 GB RAM for CPU-based inference\n- 24 GB VRAM for GPU-based inference\n\n## Competitive Comparison\n\nThe README includes a comparison table:\n\n| Model | Parameters | Context | Coding | Free |\n|-------|------------|---------|--------|------|\n| Kimi K3 | 2.8T | 1M | Top tier | This app |\n| Claude Sonnet 5 | Unknown | 200K | Top tier | Separate app |\n| GPT-5.6 | Unknown | 128K | Strong | Paid |\n| DeepSeek V4 | 671B | 128K | Strong | Separate |\n\n## Pricing and Availability\n\nPricing is described as \"significantly lower than OpenAI and Anthropic\" with a built-in free tier. The key advantage emphasized is the 1M token context window versus competitors' smaller windows (200K for Claude, 128K for GPT-5.6).",
