        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "# Crap Comment Nuker (ccn) Overview\n\n**ccn** is an interactive command-line tool that removes comments from source code across multiple programming languages. The tool uses real parsers rather than regex to safely identify and strip comments without affecting code.\n\n## Core Safety Feature\n\nThe tool's primary value proposition is that \"it cannot eat your code.\" It implements a write gate that re-parses files after modification and rejects any edit that would move even a single token. Since comments are not tokens in abstract syntax trees, your code remains untouched even if the tool makes mistakes.\n\n## Supported Languages\n\n- JavaScript/TypeScript/TSX (uses Acorn parser)\n- Python, Java, Kotlin, Rust\n- C and C++\n\nEach language covers multiple file extensions—for example, JavaScript handles `.js`, `.cjs`, `.mjs`, `.esm`, and `.jsx`.\n\n## How It Works\n\nThe tool walks through source files interactively, presenting each comment block on a cleared screen where you decide whether to remove it. You can:\n\n- Remove comments one at a time\n- Use the \"simulurity\" feature to cluster similar comments\n- Apply decisions automatically with the `--remember` flag\n- Preview changes with `--dry-run`\n\nThe tool categorizes comments with color coding: green warnings for potentially meaningful comments (those with TODO/FIXME markers or positioned above declarations), and red for standard comments.\n\n## Installation and Use\n\nInstall via npm:\n```\nnpm install -g commentnuker\n```\n\nRun interactively to review comments, or use flags to automate the process.\n\n## Notable Features\n\n- Recaps history of removed comments\n- Creates `.bak` backup files\n- Works offline after one-time parser downloads\n- Preserves HTML, Markdown, JSON, and unrecognized files\n\n## License\n\nThe tool is source-available (not OSI open source) and requires attribution for use, particularly noting \"Built with Crap Comment Nuker from justcalljon.pro\" or similar wording. Commercial use requires a separate license from Hardwick Software Services."
      }
    ]
