        "content": "Based on the repository content extracted, here's what I found about codeguard-ai:\n\n## Project Overview\n\n**codeguard-ai** is an \"AI-powered developer productivity tool for intelligent GitHub pull request review and automated test generation.\"\n\n## What It Does\n\nThe tool focuses on two primary functions:\n\n1. **Intelligent Pull Request Review** - Uses AI to analyze and review code changes in GitHub PRs\n2. **Automated Test Generation** - Automatically generates tests for code changes\n\n## Repository Structure\n\nThe project contains:\n\n- **Backend** directory (server-side components)\n- **Frontend** directory (client-side interface)\n- **AGENT.md** and **AGENTS_AND_SKILLS.md** (agent documentation)\n- **ARCHITECTURE.md** (system design documentation)\n- GitHub workflow configurations\n- Environment configuration (.env)\n\n## Technical Details\n\n- **License**: MIT License\n- **Live Demo**: Available at codeguard-ai-six.vercel.app\n- **Repository Owner**: OutDuke\n- **Current Branch**: main\n- **Commit History**: 9 commits at time of extraction\n\n## Integration\n\nThe tool appears designed to integrate directly with GitHub's workflow systems, utilizing the `.github/workflows` directory for automation and the `.specify` directory for specifications.\n\n---\n\n*Note: The repository content provided is limited to the file structure and basic descriptions. Detailed implementation specifics, API documentation, and feature guides would need to be extracted from the actual documentation files (AGENT.md, ARCHITECTURE.md, etc.) which weren't fully accessible in the provided content.*"
