    "result": "# Bastet Agent OS: Local-First AI Agent Orchestration System\n\n## Overview\n\nBastet is a \"local-first operating system for AI-agent teams\" that serves as a control plane for organizing multiple AI coding agents into teams with roles, gated workflows, and centralized governance. Unlike agent frameworks, Bastet focuses on orchestration and governance rather than being a runtime itself.\n\n## Core Purpose\n\nBastet addresses challenges in running teams of coding agents across multiple projects:\n- Failing tests typically halt workflows awaiting human intervention\n- Difficulty tracking what ran, at what cost, and on whose account\n- Each project starts from zero without retained knowledge\n- Credentials scattered across configuration files\n- Uncertainty about tool version currency\n\n## Key Features\n\n**Self-Healing Workflow Engine**\n- Stage pipelines (plan → implement → test → review → merge) with four gate types\n- Failed gates automatically route work back to appropriate stages\n- Vendor quota failures park with parsed reset times and auto-resume\n- Only stops for human intervention when genuinely unable to proceed\n\n**Project Lifecycle Management**\n- States: planning → ready → running ⇄ paused → maintenance → closed\n- State machine with only declared transitions, each audited\n- Run/pause/stop controls on project cards\n\n**Kanban Board with Real-Time Updates**\n- Task cards move across stage columns via WebSocket\n- In-progress cards show stage progress bars and heartbeat indicators\n- Human approvals include screenshots and summaries from agent preview directories\n\n**Resource Pool and Metering Gateway**\n- LLM/MCP/API/skill/git resources with visibility scopes (global/team/project)\n- Credential storage using references rather than copies\n- OpenAI/Claude-compatible gateway with usage metering\n- Real test buttons per resource type\n\n**Team Memory Integration**\n- Built on Agent Memory OS\n- Every run records actions, gate rejections, and job completion\n- Memory attributed to the specific agent that performed work\n- ACL-scoped context packs\n\n**Chat-Based Interaction**\n- Plan projects through conversation with agents or pool LLMs\n- Configure Bastet via chat interface\n- Telegram support for inline approvals and previews\n\n**Automated Delivery**\n- Completions commit to job-specific `bastet/<job_id>` branches\n- Pushes to project remotes using project credentials\n- Human-controlled merging\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe system comprises:\n\n```\nWebUI (React) ───┤\nCLI (Typer) ───┤ FastAPI: REST + WebSocket event bus │\nTelegram ───┤ auth: api token · user tokens · roles │\n\nOrchestrator │ stages · gates │ rework loop │\nGateway /v1/* │ OpenAI + Anthropic │ metering, budgets │\nExecutor plugin │ claude-code │ claude-sdk │ codex · grok │ agy · hermes │\ngit worktree or container per run │\n\nSQLite (WAL): projects · jobs · runs · gates │\nusage_ledger · grants · audit_log (hash chain) │\n\nAgent Memory OS: team/project ACL, context packs │\n```\n\n## Comparison Table\n\n| Aspect | Bastet | Agent Frameworks | Hosted Platforms |\n|--------|--------|------------------|------------------|\n| What | Control plane over existing agents | Runtime itself | Their runtime |\n| Where | Your machine/LAN | Your process | Their cloud |\n| Execution | Delegates to external agents | You write the loop | Their loop |\n| On failure | Routes back to fixable stage | Your code decides | Opaque |\n| Accounting | Usage ledger + audit log | None | Their dashboard |\n| Memory | AMOS with ACL | None/bring your own | Their store |\n| Credentials | Single reference point | Your config | Uploaded |\n\n## Installation\n\nAvailable via:\n```bash\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yamantaka520/Bastet-Agent-OS/main/install.sh | bash\n```\n\nOr from PyPI or Docker Hub:\n```bash\npip install bastet-agent-os\ndocker run -v bastet:/data -p 8890:8890 yamantaka520/bastet-agent-os\n```\n\n## Supported Agents\n\n- Claude Code (CLI or Agent SDK)\n- Codex CLI\n- Grok Build\n- Google Antigravity (agy)\n- Hermes\n- Any OpenAI/Claude-compatible endpoint\n\n## Development Status\n\nAll milestones M0-M6 complete, including federation, self-healing workflows, and multi-user authentication. Validated on Ubuntu 26.04 with Python 3.14.\n\n## License\n\nApache-2.0, built on Agent Memory OS.",
    "durationMs": 17123,
    "url": "https://github.com/yamantaka520/Bastet-Agent-OS"
  }
}

