code\",\n      \"Uses real parsers rather than regex for safety\",\n      \"Write gate re-parses and rejects token-moving edits\",\n      \"9 languages, one tool\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Benzi\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/shobhitx64/Benzi\",\n    \"description\": \"AI coding agent and harness that compiles codebases into resolved maps before analysis instead of dumping files into context windows. Creates structured maps containing calls, data flow, and references, then navigates with real tools. Supports Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, Java, C#, C++, C, Go, Rust, and Ruby with three-tier truth system (proven/candidate/runtime-observed edges), runtime tracer for real argument values, model-agnostic design supporting Anthropic/OpenAI APIs, persistent per-repo memory, and dual-engine for code and markup. Edits are syntax-gated using real language parsers with auto-revert and blast radius reporting.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-07-29\",\n    \"category\": \"AI coding CLI\",\n    \"sources\": [\"GitHub\", \"Show HN\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\n      \"AI coding agent that doesn't guess — it reads\",\n      \"Compiles codebases into resolved maps before analysis\",\n      \"Indexes the full resolved structure\",\n      \"Beating Claude Code itself on Sonnet\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Bastet Agent OS\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/yamantaka520/Bastet-Agent-OS\",\n    \"description\": \"Local-first control plane for AI-agent teams that orchestrates Claude Code, Codex, Grok, agy, and Hermes into gated workflows with self-healing capabilities. Features stage pipelines (plan→implement→test→review→merge) with four gate types, failed gates routing back to appropriate stages, vendor quota failure handling with auto-resume, per-run metering, append-only audit log, and team memory built on Agent Memory OS. Includes project lifecycle management, Kanban board with real-time WebSocket updates, resource pool with credential storage, and chat-based configuration with Telegram support for inline approvals.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-07-28\",\n    \"category\": \"workflow agent\",\n    \"sources\": [\"GitHub\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\n      \"Local-first control plane for AI-agent teams\",\n      \"Orchestrates Claude Code, Codex, Grok, agy & Hermes into gated workflows\",\n      \"Self-healing workflows that fix their own failures\",\n      \"Per-run metering, audit log, and team memory\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Antigravity CLI VS Code Extension\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/Nuwanthapasindu/antigravity-cli-vs-code-extension\",\n    \"description\": \"VS Code extension that integrates the agy (Antigravity CLI) AI coding assistant directly into the editor environment. Opens agy as a right-side editor panel keeping code visible on left and AI assistant on right, mirroring the UX of Claude Code and Codex extensions. Features Activity Bar icon, right-side terminal, top-right editor button, status bar indicator, keyboard shortcut (Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+A), smart terminal reuse focus, auto-close on /exit, and configurable agy path and launch arguments. Version 0.0.2 added drag-and-drop file support with Shift-key absolute path pasting.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-07-28\",\n    \"category\": \"IDE integration\",\n    \"sources\": [\"GitHub\", \"VS Code Marketplace\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\n      \"VS Code extension for Antigravity CLI (agy)\",\n      \"Opens as right-side panel like Claude Code and Codex\",\n      \"No need to switch to separate terminal window\",\n      \"Drag-and-drop files to add to CLI context\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Ponytail\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/0xwilliamortiz/ponytail-improved\",\n    \"description\": \"AI coding agent skill that prevents over-engineering by implementing a decision ladder forcing agents to evaluate options before writing code: (1) Does this need to exist? (2) Is it already in this repo? (3) Does standard